The query-normalization logic, proxy handling, feature set and overall architecture
were adapted from that project. It has been substantially rewritten: listings are
parsed from catalog HTML via curl_cffi (instead of the now bot-protected JSON API),
novelty is id-based, the runtime is a single threaded process (instead of the original
multiprocessing design), and it adds a new Flask dashboard, ntfy support and silent
first-scrape seeding.
